//  PETPORTS -- ZESTY PET TREAT
//
//  A flavoured Pet Treat. The upcycler produces these when a Living Root-class
//  reagent is in its reagent slot; see scripts/lofty_petports/petports_flavours.config
//  for the reagent list and what each one is worth.
//
//  FLAVOUR IS THE WHOLE OF THE PREFERENCE SYSTEM. A unit rolls one preferred
//  flavour and refills more of its fuel bar eating that one. Every other
//  flavour, and the unflavoured treat, are worth exactly the same to it -- so
//  feeding a unit the wrong flavour is never a mistake, only a missed bonus.
//  That is what keeps reagents optional rather than a chore.
//
//  A SEPARATE ITEM NAME, NOT A PARAMETER ON petports_petfuel. The whole sorting
//  system keys on names, so distinct names mean a player can route spicy into
//  one crate and sweet into another with the filters that already exist. A
//  parameter would have made the census sum every flavour as one item, which is
//  right for thresholds and wrong for storage.
//
//  PRICE ZERO, AND IT IS LOAD-BEARING. The upcycler values its input by price
//  and refuses anything tagged petports_no_upcycling. Both guards are here for
//  the same reason the unflavoured treat has them: a treat worth anything is a
//  treat that can be fed back in, and a laundering loop that pays out slowly is
//  harder to notice than one that pays out fast.
//
//  petports_fuel IS WHAT THE FILTER MANIFEST MATCHES ON, by tag rather than by
//  name, so this sorts into the Pet Treats subgroup without the manifest being
//  edited. Do not drop that tag: fuelWork only sends a unit to empty an
//  upcycler's output slot when some deposit beacon accepts what is in it, so an
//  untagged treat fills a machine and stops it.
//
//  PLACEHOLDER ART: the unflavoured treat's flat square in this flavour's
//  colour. Obviously unfinished on purpose, so it cannot be mistaken for a
//  design decision. The colours themselves are NOT placeholder -- they are
//  spread across lightness as well as hue so the seven stay distinguishable
//  under red-green colour blindness, where a naive palette collapses spicy into
//  zesty and savory. Keep that spread when the real art lands.

{
	"itemName" : "petports_petfuel_zesty",
	"price" : 0,
	"rarity" : "Common",
	"category" : "petports_fuel",
	"inventoryIcon" : "petports_petfuel_zesty.png",
	"description" : "Pressed surplus, run through with root and green things. The closest a utility unit gets to a salad.",
	"shortdescription" : "Zesty Pet Treat",
	"itemTags" : [ "petports", "petports_fuel", "petports_no_upcycling" ],
	"maxStack" : 1000
}
